menu "SempreIoT firmware update (siot_ota_board, siot_ota_node)"

    config SIOT_FEATURE_OTA
        bool "Firmware update over the link and the mesh (protocol section 13)"
        default y
        help
            Board: takes an image from the tablet, updates itself, hands a
            stored image to the units. Node: takes the board's offer. On by
            default, unlike the other features: every product image must be
            updatable. The options below are the same for the board and the
            node.

    config SIOT_OTA_TEST_ANY_VERSION
        bool "TEST ONLY: accept any version (the same one again, an older one)"
        default y
        help
            *** MUST BE OFF IN PRODUCTION — docs/ota/before-production.md, item 1. ***

            Protocol section 13.2: a unit installs an image only when its
            version is NEWER than the one it runs. That rule is what stops an
            old, vulnerable release from being put back on a unit. It is
            switched off here, on purpose, since 2026-09-29, so the same test
            image can be pushed over and over on the bench.

            firmware/ci/check.sh --release refuses to pass while this is on.

    config SIOT_OTA_ALLOW_FORCE
        bool "Bench: honour FORCE (install an older or the same version)"
        default n
        help
            Protocol section 13.2. A production build leaves this off and
            answers FORCE_REFUSED. Turn it on for a bench board that must be
            taken back to an older image over the link.

    config SIOT_OTA_SELFTEST_FAIL
        bool "Bench: this image fails its self-test (rollback test, check O4)"
        default n
        help
            A board image built with this on never confirms itself: 120 s
            after it boots from an update the board goes back to the image it
            ran before. Never release a build with this on.

    config SIOT_OTA_SELFTEST_S
        int "Seconds a new board image has to pass its self-test"
        default 120
        range 20 600

endmenu
